=== SLH-DSA Integration Demonstration ===

=== SLH-DSA Structure ===

SLH-DSA combines three main components:

1. FORS (Forest of Random Subsets)
   - Few-time signature scheme
   - Signs the message digest directly
   - Reveals k secret values from k trees

2. XMSS (eXtended Merkle Signature Scheme)
   - One tree = many one-time signatures
   - Uses WOTS+ as the one-time signature
   - Merkle tree aggregates WOTS+ public keys

3. Hypertree
   - Stack of XMSS trees
   - Each layer signs the layer below
   - Allows huge number of signatures
   - Height H = d * h' where d=layers, h'=per-layer height

Security: Based on hash function security
   - Pre-image resistance
   - Second pre-image resistance
   - Collision resistance
   - Post-quantum secure (no lattice/number theory)

